S({
  id: 'b12_ribs', ch: 'shell', theme: 'night', title: 'Ribs as deep as the mould can fill', settle: 12.5, ideas: [75, 5],
  after: 'b12_latopt',
  src: ['b12Study', 'b05Ji', 'b05Ucsb', 'b12Beall', 'b12Dfm', 'b12Proto', 'b12Xometry', 'b12Strat', 'b12Shrink', 'b12Edm', 'b05Mit', 'shlEnvalior', 'beall106'],
  answers: [
    ['F45.1 "the codex version had a good demo with a ruler ... structure of material matters more than weight"', 'Called back, not repeated (b05_cubed shows the ruler in full): the strip turns on its edge, 9.1× stiffer at the same 2.00 g; a rib is that ruler standing on the skin.'],
    ['F45.2 "this could be tied into the how the dimensions of the beams in lattice/interwoven arches are chosen"', 'The rib is swept deeper on the whole shell at the same weight: the flex falls as it deepens (the ruler\'s law), until the mould\'s limit at three skins deep, where the chosen rib sits.'],
    ['F45.2 "also keep manufacturability in mind when you choose dimensions"', 'Every dimension is bounded by a cited limit drawn on the slide: depth three skins (Beall 2000, DFMPro; the stricter three rib widths dashed, Xometry, Stratasys Direct), width 60 % of the skin against sink (Protolabs, Xometry; PP-C-20A shrinks little), draft 0.5° (DFMPro), the root fillet inside the 0.25 to 0.4 skins band (DFMPro), the skin 0.60 mm (as on the plate, F20.3).'],
    ['F43.4 "... and filet size"', 'Two fillets, both named. At the root, in section, solved on this rib: the stress factor falls steeply until about a quarter skin and hardly after, while the joint thickens toward a sink; on this shell the root stays under the rib\'s own peak anywhere in the guides\' 0.25 to 0.4 skins, so the mould sets it: ' + (B12 ? fmtN(B12.win.rPick, 2) : '0.24') + ' mm, the top of the band. Where ribs cross, in plan: ' + (B12 ? fmtN(B12.win.rNode, 2) : '0.22') + ' mm, b06_filletsize\'s rule (60 % of the strut) scaled to the 0.36 mm rib.'],
    ['R3-b12-2 (the 0.89 mm floor) and Brock\'s "Skin: 0.60 mm, to be proven" (12:10)', 'Said once on the slide: the 0.60 mm skin is a target to prove by a mould-flow check or first shots at the chin\'s rim, the farthest point (about 105 mm from the gate, 175 skins; polypropylene runs 150 to 280, MIT 2.008); the ribs three skins deep likewise (Beall 2000; the stricter three rib widths drawn, with what the extra depth buys, R3-b12-5). Worded with P4, who restates b05_wall and b06 on the same rule (flow length for the skin; Protolabs\'s 0.889 / 0.635 mm as rules of thumb, not a floor).'],
    ['Brock (relayed ~13:3x): "1.80, cut steel-safe"; R3-b12-5 (the 1.80 mm rib is five rib widths deep)', 'The 1.80 mm target stays, and its tooling plan is one line under the depth chart: the mould is cut 1.5 mm deep first and deepened to 1.8 after trial shots, because removing steel is easy and adding it isn\'t. Beside the stricter guides\' dashed three-rib-widths line (with the flex that depth would give, marked on the curve), it says why the rib goes past that guide and how the risk is held: a target, cut safe and proven in the trial.']
  ],
  draw: t => {
    header(t, 'Ribs as deep as the mould can fill');
    if (!B12) return;
    const R = B12_R, win = B12.win, base = B12.base;
    captions(t, [[0.3, 'A rib is the ruler on its edge: depth counts cubed, so every rib in the study wanted to be deeper.'],
      [R.d0, 'At the same weight the skin thins to pay for depth: shallow ribs lose to a plain wall, deep ones win, until the mould says stop at three skins.'],
      [R.f0, 'The root\'s fillet is set by the mould: past a quarter skin its stress hardly falls while the joint thickens toward a sink, so ' + fmtN(win.rPick, 2) + ' mm.']]);
    /* ---------------- left top: the ruler again (b05_cubed's numbers) ---------------- */
    const R5 = typeof B05_C !== 'undefined' ? B05_C : null, rK = R5 ? R5.rulerK : 9.18, rg = R5 ? R5.ruler.g : 2.0;
    const pr = demoPanel(t, -1, [LM, 280, 640, 230], { label: 'Try it with a ruler', src: 'Ji, Manchester; UCSB' });   /* V3: the film's one ruler (F45.1) */
    { const k = ep(t, 0.5, 1.6, E.io3), th = k * Math.PI / 2, cx = pr[0] + 90, cy = pr[1] + 70;
      G.save(); G.translate(cx, cy); G.rotate(th); rr(-10 * 4, -3.3 * 4, 20 * 4, 6.6 * 4, 2, mix(C.hero, C.bg, 0.25), C.hero, 2, 1); G.restore();
      text(k < 0.5 ? 'Flat' : 'On edge', cx, cy + 66, { role: 'label', size: 19, color: k < 0.5 ? C.mute : C.heroText, align: 'center' });
      const ks = ep(t, 1.5, 1.9);
      rich([{ s: b12_dn(rK, 1) + '×', font: 'disp', size: 44, weight: 800, color: C.heroText, grad: C.heroGrad, caps: false }, { s: 'stiffer on edge,', role: 'small', size: 22, weight: 650, color: C.ink2, gap: 14, sentence: false }], pr[0] + 190, cy - 16, { alpha: ks });
      text('the same ' + fmtN(rg, 2) + ' g', pr[0] + 190 + 98, cy + 14, { role: 'small', size: 22, weight: 650, color: C.ink2, alpha: ks, sentence: false });
      text('A rib is that ruler, standing on the skin.', pr[0] + 190, cy + 52, { role: 'small', size: 21, weight: 600, color: C.mute, alpha: ep(t, 1.9, 2.3), maxW: pr[2] - 190 }); }
    /* ---------------- left bottom: the rib, to scale, its depth swept at the same weight ---------------- */
    const h = b12_depth(t), f = b12_dAt(h), lim = 3 * f[1], rt = b12_fil(t), rr0 = rt * f[1];
    const sx = LM, sy = 550, sw = 640, sh = 410, a2 = tileA(t, -2, 1);
    demoWindow(sx, sy, sw, sh, a2);
    text('One rib on the skin, to scale (×' + 58 + ')', sx + 28, sy + 46, { role: 'label', size: 20, color: C.mute, alpha: a2 });
    { const s = 58, x0 = sx + 214, y0 = sy + sh - 132;
      b12_ribSec(x0, y0, s, f[1], f[2], h, rr0, { hBad: lim, span: 1.75 });
      /* the limit: three skins deep, dashed across the rib */
      const yl = y0 - (f[1] + lim) * s, kl = ep(t, R.d0 + 0.4, R.d0 + 0.8);
      line(x0 - 50, yl, x0 + 50, yl, { color: C.mute, w: 1.5, dash: [5, 4], alpha: kl });
      text('3 skins', x0 + 56, yl + 7, { role: 'small', size: 19, weight: 650, color: C.mute, alpha: kl, sentence: false });
      /* the width and the draft, named at the rib */
      const kw = ep(t, 1.2, 1.6), yw = y0 - (f[1] + 0.35) * s;
      text('60 % of the skin', x0 - 34, yw, { role: 'small', size: 19, weight: 650, color: C.ink2, align: 'right', alpha: kw, sentence: false });
      text('0.5° draft', x0 - 34, yw - 30, { role: 'small', size: 19, weight: 650, color: C.ink2, align: 'right', alpha: kw, sentence: false });
      /* readouts: a 2 x 2 grid right of the rib */
      const ox = sx + 352, ox2 = ox + 150, ro = (lab, x, yy) => text(lab, x, yy, { role: 'label', size: 19, color: C.mute, maxW: 146 });
      const bad = h > lim + 0.02;
      ro('Rib depth', ox, sy + 80); text(fmtN(h, 2) + ' mm', ox, sy + 116, { font: 'disp', size: 36, weight: 800, color: bad ? C.bad : C.heroText, grad: bad ? null : C.heroGrad, tnum: true });
      ro('Skin', ox, sy + 154); text(fmtN(f[1], 2) + ' mm', ox, sy + 186, { font: 'disp', size: 28, weight: 800, color: f[1] < 0.594 ? C.bad : C.ink, tnum: true });
      ro('Rib width', ox2, sy + 154); text(fmtN(f[2], 2) + ' mm', ox2, sy + 186, { font: 'disp', size: 28, weight: 800, color: C.ink, tnum: true });
      ro('Root fillet', ox, sy + 224); text(fmtN(rr0, 2) + ' mm', ox, sy + 256, { font: 'disp', size: 28, weight: 800, color: C.ink, tnum: true });
      ro('Node fillet', ox2, sy + 224); text(fmtN(win.rNode, 2) + ' mm', ox2, sy + 256, { font: 'disp', size: 28, weight: 800, color: C.ink, tnum: true });
      text('in section', ox, sy + 280, { role: 'small', size: 19, weight: 600, color: C.faint, sentence: false }); text('in plan', ox2, sy + 280, { role: 'small', size: 19, weight: 600, color: C.faint, sentence: false });
      /* why a 0.60 mm skin and a 0.36 mm rib fill: two different rules (R3-b12-2) */
      const fl = B12.flow, kf2 = ep(t, 1.6, 2.0);
      if (fl) text('Targets to prove in the mould: the 0.60 mm skin (the melt runs about ' + fmtN(fl.mm, 0) + ' mm to the chin\'s rim, ' + fmtN(fl.mm / 0.6, 0) + ' skins; polypropylene runs 150 to 280, MIT 2.008) and ribs three skins deep (Beall 2000; stricter guides say three rib widths). A mould-flow check or first shots settle both.', sx + 28, sy + sh - 100, { role: 'small', size: 19, weight: 600, color: C.mute, maxW: sw - 56, alpha: kf2, sentence: false, lh: 1.2 });
      if (bad) text('Deeper than three skins: it may not fill', sx + 28, sy + 80, { role: 'small', size: 19, weight: 650, color: C.bad, maxW: 300 }); }
    /* ---------------- right top: flex against depth, with the mould's limits ---------------- */
    const cx0 = LM + 680, cy0 = 280, cw = RM - cx0, ch = 400, a3 = tileA(t, -2, 2);
    demoWindow(cx0, cy0, cw, ch, a3);
    text('Flex under the worst hard press as the rib deepens, same 9.35 g', cx0 + 28, cy0 + 46, { role: 'label', size: 19, color: C.mute, alpha: a3, maxW: cw - 180 });
    pill(cx0 + cw - 28 - pillW('derived'), cy0 + 46, 'derived', a3);
    const D = B12.depth, yMin = Math.floor((Math.min.apply(null, D.map(r => r[3])) - 4) / 20) * 20, yMax = Math.ceil((Math.max(base.worst, D[0][3]) + 4) / 20) * 20;
    const M = axes(t, { x: cx0 + 100, y: cy0 + 92, w: cw - 150, h: ch - 214, xr: [0.4, 2.8], yr: [yMin, yMax], xticks: [0.6, 1.0, 1.4, 1.8, 2.2, 2.6], yticks: Array.from({ length: Math.round((yMax - yMin) / 20) + 1 }, (_, i) => yMin + 20 * i), xfmt: v => fmtN(v, 1), yfmt: v => v + ' µm', t0: -2 });
    text('Rib depth, mm', cx0 + cw - 50, cy0 + ch - 30, { role: 'label', size: 19, color: C.mute, align: 'right', alpha: a3 });
    /* the tooling plan for the 1.80 mm target (Brock, ~13:2x: "1.80, cut steel-safe"): it also answers the stricter guides' line */
    text('The mould is cut 1.5 mm deep first and deepened to 1.8 after trial shots: removing steel is easy, adding it isn\'t.', cx0 + 28, cy0 + ch - 54, { role: 'small', size: 19, weight: 650, color: C.ink2, maxW: cw - 240, lh: 1.25, sentence: false, alpha: ep(t, R.d0 + 1.0, R.d0 + 1.4) });
    const hLim = win.hr, h3w = 3 * win.w, kL = ep(t, R.d0 + 0.4, R.d0 + 0.8);
    rect(M.X(hLim), M.Y(yMax), M.X(2.8) - M.X(hLim), M.Y(yMin) - M.Y(yMax), { fill: rgba(C.bad, 0.12), alpha: kL });
    text('Too deep to fill', (M.X(hLim) + M.X(2.8)) / 2, M.Y(yMax) - 12, { role: 'label', size: 19, color: C.bad, align: 'center', alpha: kL });
    text('Past 3 skins (Beall 2000, DFMPro), and the skin under 0.60 mm', M.X(hLim) + 12, M.Y(yMax) + 26, { role: 'small', size: 19, weight: 600, color: C.bad, alpha: kL, maxW: M.X(2.8) - M.X(hLim) - 20, lh: 1.2 });
    const k3 = ep(t, R.d0 + 0.9, R.d0 + 1.3);
    line(M.X(h3w), M.Y(yMax), M.X(h3w), M.Y(yMin), { color: C.mute, w: 1.5, dash: [5, 5], alpha: k3 });
    text('Stricter guides: 3 rib widths', M.X(h3w) + 10, M.Y(yMin) - 38, { role: 'label', size: 19, color: C.mute, alpha: k3 });
    /* what the extra depth buys: the flex at the stricter guides' depth, on the curve (R3-b12-5) */
    if (b12_hasDepth() && t >= R.d0 && b12_depthMax(t) >= h3w) { const f3 = b12_dAt(h3w)[3]; circle(M.X(h3w), M.Y(f3), 6, { fill: C.comp, alpha: k3 }); text(fmtN(f3, 0) + ' µm', M.X(h3w) - 12, M.Y(f3) + 7, { role: 'num', size: 22, weight: 800, color: C.ink2, align: 'right', alpha: k3 }); }
    text('Xometry, Stratasys', M.X(h3w) + 10, M.Y(yMin) - 12, { role: 'small', size: 19, weight: 600, color: C.mute, alpha: k3, sentence: false });
    line(M.X(0.4), M.Y(base.worst), M.X(2.8), M.Y(base.worst), { color: C.comp, w: 2, dash: [7, 6], alpha: ep(t, 1.0, 1.4) });
    text('A plain wall, same weight', M.X(1.16), M.Y(base.worst) - 10, { role: 'small', size: 19, weight: 600, color: C.mute, alpha: ep(t, 1.0, 1.4) });
    const pMax = D.length > 1 ? clamp((b12_depthMax(t) - D[0][0]) / (D[D.length - 1][0] - D[0][0])) : 1;
    if (t >= R.d0) series(M, D.map(r => [r[0], r[3]]), { color: C.hero, w: 3, p: pMax });
    D.forEach(r => { if (t >= R.d0 && r[0] <= b12_depthMax(t) + 1e-6) circle(M.X(r[0]), M.Y(r[3]), 4, { fill: r[0] > hLim + 1e-3 ? C.bad : C.hero }); });
    circle(M.X(h), M.Y(f[3]), 11, { color: C.ink, w: 1.5, alpha: 0.5 }); circle(M.X(h), M.Y(f[3]), 5, { fill: C.ink });
    cursorAt(t, [[R.d1, [M.X(2.6) + 60, M.Y(f[3]) + 50]], [R.d1 + 0.3, [M.X(2.6) + 3, M.Y(b12_dAt(2.6)[3]) + 3]], [R.back[1], [M.X(win.hr) + 3, M.Y(win.worst) + 3]], [R.back[1] + 0.4, [M.X(win.hr) + 3, M.Y(win.worst) + 3]]], [R.d1 + 0.35], { a: ep(t, R.d1 - 0.1, R.d1 + 0.2) * (1 - ep(t, R.back[1] + 0.2, R.back[1] + 0.5)), grab: t > R.d1 + 0.3 && t < R.back[1] + 0.05 });
    /* ---------------- right bottom: the root fillet, solved on this rib ---------------- */
    const fx0 = cx0, fy0 = cy0 + ch + 40, fw = cw, fh = 960 - fy0, a4 = tileA(t, -2, 3);
    demoWindow(fx0, fy0, fw, fh, a4);
    text('The root fillet, in section: its peak at 10 N, against the rib\'s own', fx0 + 28, fy0 + 44, { role: 'label', size: 19, color: C.mute, alpha: a4, maxW: fw - 60 });
    { const F = B12.fil, rp = win.rootNom, sp = win.beamPeak, tS = B12.filsec ? B12.filsec[0] : win.t;
      const Mf0 = axes(t, { x: fx0 + 100, y: fy0 + 80, w: fw - 150, h: fh - 162, xr: [0, 0.45], yr: [0, 0.2], xticks: [0, 0.1, 0.2, 0.3, 0.4], yticks: [0, 0.1, 0.2], xfmt: v => fmtN(v, 1), yfmt: v => fmtN(v * 100, 0) + ' %', t0: -2 });
      const Mf = { X: v => Mf0.X(v * tS), Y: Mf0.Y };       /* the curve's own unit is the share of the skin (r / t) */
      const kb = ep(t, R.f0 - 0.4, R.f0);
      rect(Mf.X(0.25), Mf.Y(0.2), Mf.X(0.4) - Mf.X(0.25), Mf.Y(0) - Mf.Y(0.2), { fill: C.heroSoft, alpha: kb });
      text('Guides: 0.25 to 0.4 skins', (Mf.X(0.25) + Mf.X(0.4)) / 2, Mf.Y(0.2) - 10, { role: 'label', size: 19, color: C.heroText, align: 'center', alpha: kb });
      rect(Mf.X(0.4), Mf.Y(0.2), Mf.X(0.75) - Mf.X(0.4), Mf.Y(0) - Mf.Y(0.2), { fill: rgba(C.bad, 0.10), alpha: kb });
      text('Thicker junction: sinks', (Mf.X(0.4) + Mf.X(0.75)) / 2, Mf.Y(0.2) - 10, { role: 'label', size: 19, color: C.bad, align: 'center', alpha: kb });
      line(Mf.X(0), Mf.Y(sp), Mf.X(0.75), Mf.Y(sp), { color: C.comp, w: 2, dash: [7, 6], alpha: kb });
      text('The rib itself: ' + fmtN(sp * 100, 0) + ' %', Mf.X(0.74), Mf.Y(sp) - 10, { role: 'small', size: 19, weight: 600, color: C.mute, align: 'right', alpha: kb });
      const curve = F.filter(r => r[0] >= 0.05 && r[0] <= 0.75).map(r => [r[0], rp * r[1]]);
      series(Mf, curve, { color: C.hero, w: 3, p: clamp((b12_filMax(t) - 0.05) / 0.7) });
      if (t >= R.f0) { const sc = b12_scf(rt)[0]; circle(Mf.X(rt), Mf.Y(rp * sc), 9, { color: C.ink, w: 1.5, alpha: 0.5 }); circle(Mf.X(rt), Mf.Y(rp * sc), 4.5, { fill: C.ink }); }
      text('Root fillet radius, mm', fx0 + fw - 50, fy0 + fh - 14, { role: 'label', size: 19, color: C.mute, align: 'right', alpha: a4 }); }
    source(t, 'The 3D shell study (every design 9.35 g); the fillet: plane-strain FE on this rib. Guides: Beall 2000, DFMPro, Protolabs, Xometry, Stratasys Direct.', { t0: 0.8, y: 998 });
  }
});
